execution/v2.4/commands.json:1201:      "note": "registered by W13-01: check_id W13-01 is served by tests/ui/check/main.py, which drives lib/host.js and lib/ipc.js through node with injected fakes. Every other selector this key resolves, including case C23 which the v2.0 entry already serves, is forwarded unchanged to ops/ci/ui.py --phase workflow with the same selector environment, so binding this card cannot shadow an accepted binding. The branch choice is asserted as W1301-ROUTING-TRUTH-TABLE and the forwarded row is re-measured in binding_and_parity_rev15_at_head.json. Disclosed consequence, corrected in round 3 after two reviews flagged the old sentence as false: the forwarded branch does not resolve python through PATH - the dispatcher launches the check program from the locked toolchain table and main.py forwards with sys.executable, which is that same pinned build. The forwarded row is re-measured in binding_and_parity_rev15_at_head.json, the file the receipt quotes; binding_and_parity_rev15.json is kept only as the binding-commit provenance and its local row predates the suite reaching 29 assertions."
